 e:"In Stage 1 part of the thickened flotation tails went to the old CIL2/CIL3 and the rest straight to the TSF, and some concentrate was still filtered and trucked to the offsite roaster. In Stage 2 all thickened tails go to CIL4 and all concentrate is treated at FIM. The drawings carry legends like 'SP1 AS BUILT' and 'SP2 NEW / SP2 DECOMMISSIONED'. SP means Separable Portion, the contract packages for Stage 1 and Stage 2.",
